I apologize for the mistake, the above assert statements are wrong. The correct ones are:

<code>
Debug.Assert(New_Ret <= Old_arrListCount);
</code>
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == Old_arrListCount + 1);
</code>
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == New_arrListCount);
</code>
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == New_arrListIndexOfX || New_Ret == Old_arrListIndexOfX);
</code>
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == New_arrListLastIndexOfX || New_Ret == Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);
</code>
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_Ret >= 0);
</code>

<code>
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == Old_arrListCount + 1);
</code>
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == New_arrListCount);
</code>
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == true && New_arrListContainsX == New_Ret != -1);
</code>

Please note that the above assertions are based on the assumptions about the behavior of the `Add` method of `ArrayList`. As `Add` method adds an element to the end of the list, it should increase the Count property of the list and return the new Count.
